Upstream-bound: no
Subject: [PORT_HOST] P6.18 Instant: lines that scroll in a text appear whole, after a short hold

Patch 0063 shows a dialogue page whole at its start in Instant mode, but the
game's window shows two lines of a three line text and then scrolls: when the
page is full (textCodeNewLine, lineCount >= lines) the window moves up one
line and the new line is typed at the fast delay, one character every three
frames. A long line takes 3 frames per character: the owner's OLED log
(preview.30-rc4, Instant, EU) has pages that took 103 and 127 frames to type
(34 and 42 characters), after every battle, so Instant was not instant there.

With the Text speed option at Instant, textCodeNewLine now asks the port
(dw3_port_pacing_text_scroll) what to do at the scroll point:

* hold (1): draw nothing further this frame and leave the window as it is.
  The newline code is met again next frame, so the full page stays on screen
  for DW3_PACING_SCROLL_HOLD frames before it scrolls. Without the hold, the
  lines shown would be replaced a few frames after they appear and could not
  be read.
* scroll and reveal (2): the scroll as the game does it, then
  textWindowShowPage so the new line is on screen at once.

The cost of a scrolled line is therefore the hold (12 frames), whatever its
length, instead of 3 frames per character. Normal and Fast, and every window
that does not type at the fast dialogue delay (the area banner, windows that
type at 0), get 0 and run the game's own code, bit-identical to before. Waits
for a button and page breaks are not touched: they stop the window before this
code is reached.

--- a/src/engine/text/text_window.c
+++ b/src/engine/text/text_window.c
@@ -655,15 +655,31 @@
 
 /* Control code 1: a new line, or a new page when the page is full */
 s32 textCodeNewLine(TextWindow *obj, TextBuffer *buf, TextDraw *draw) {
+#if PORT_HOST
+    s32 scrollMode;
+#endif
     if (++draw->lineCount == 1) {
         draw->pageStart = buf->pos + 2;
     } else if (draw->lineCount >= obj->lines) {
+#if PORT_HOST
+        /* P6.18 Instant: hold the full page a moment before it scrolls (1), then
+         * show the new line at once after the scroll (2) */
+        scrollMode = dw3_port_pacing_text_scroll(obj, obj->typeDelay);
+        if (scrollMode == 1) {
+            return 0x8000;
+        }
+#endif
         obj->start = draw->pageStart;
         if (obj->lines >= 2) {
             obj->lines--;
             textWindowShowPage(obj);
             obj->lines++;
         }
+#if PORT_HOST
+        if (scrollMode == 2) {
+            textWindowShowPage(obj);
+        }
+#endif
         return 0x8000;
     }
     obj->cursorX = 0;
